1
00:00:03,603 --> 00:00:05,705
FREELANCE SURGEON
MICHIKO DAIMON

2
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:13,113
I'm about to open
the pancreatic parenchyma.

3
00:00:13,279 --> 00:00:15,048
Prep the linear stapler.

4
00:00:15,515 --> 00:00:16,516
Yes, ma'am.

5
00:00:16,583 --> 00:00:19,085
KAZUMA USHIO
HIDEKI KAJI

6
00:00:24,090 --> 00:00:26,793
- No, that's not it.
- I'm sorry.

7
00:00:34,801 --> 00:00:38,671
BP, 110 over 76. Pulse, 87, sinus.

8
00:00:38,738 --> 00:00:39,739
Done.

9
00:00:39,839 --> 00:00:40,874
Goodbye.

10
00:00:41,341 --> 00:00:43,543
She's as fast as ever.

11
00:00:44,344 --> 00:00:45,512
Dr. Daimon, I have a message

12
00:00:45,612 --> 00:00:48,448
from Assistant Director Tange
at a medical conference in Paris.

13
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:53,686
Don't just walk away!

14
00:00:53,787 --> 00:00:55,789
"My friend in making reforms, Dr. Daimon,

15
00:00:55,855 --> 00:00:59,125
I give you permission to operate
all you like in my absence.

16
00:00:59,459 --> 00:01:02,295
With love from Paris, Nicholas Tange."

17
00:01:02,629 --> 00:01:04,330
That's a Brazilian for you.

18
00:01:04,397 --> 00:01:06,699
He's even sending his love
to Michiko Daimon.

19
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,668
Yes!

20
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:13,039
I'll operate without stopping!
Let's get to it, people!

21
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:16,509
Dr. Daimon, we can't today.

22
00:01:16,709 --> 00:01:18,711
We have an important lecture to attend.

23
00:01:18,812 --> 00:01:20,346
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

24
00:01:20,547 --> 00:01:21,815
- Seriously?
- What?

25
00:01:24,384 --> 00:01:27,053
What lecture could be
more important than surgery?

26
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:29,823
While Nichotan's away,
Director Hiruma got carried away

27
00:01:30,123 --> 00:01:31,724
and invited a VIP guest.

28
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:34,094
<i>A VIP guest?</i>

29
00:01:36,763 --> 00:01:41,000
Even you can't operate without
surgical nurses, Dr. Daimon.

30
00:01:41,067 --> 00:01:42,435
That's for sure.

31
00:01:43,336 --> 00:01:45,605
- Let me do it!
- Really?

32
00:01:46,673 --> 00:01:48,708
What? You?

33
00:01:48,808 --> 00:01:51,277
I want to become
a real surgical nurse soon.

34
00:01:51,344 --> 00:01:53,079
I'll do my best as the instrument nurse.

35
00:01:53,146 --> 00:01:55,849
Being the instrument nurse requires
speed, proper judgment,

36
00:01:55,915 --> 00:01:57,750
and the ability to anticipate.

37
00:01:57,851 --> 00:01:59,853
You couldn't do it now
no matter how much you tried.

38
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:10,296
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

39
00:02:11,531 --> 00:02:16,202
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

40
00:02:16,803 --> 00:02:20,673
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

41
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:23,309
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

42
00:02:23,376 --> 00:02:27,280
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

43
00:02:29,249 --> 00:02:32,418
- Greetings.
- Greetings.

44
00:02:34,087 --> 00:02:37,257
MASAE MIHARA, HONORARY PRESIDENT
JAPANESE NURSING CONFEDERATION

45
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:41,127
It's a pleasure to see you,
Honorary President Mihara.

46
00:02:41,561 --> 00:02:42,929
It's a pleasure to see you.

47
00:02:43,763 --> 00:02:47,367
It has been a long time, Dr. Hiruma.

48
00:02:47,433 --> 00:02:50,737
Yes, it has been a while.
Thank you for coming.

49
00:02:53,373 --> 00:02:55,475
Thank you for taking the trouble to come.

50
00:02:55,608 --> 00:02:57,377
We're looking forward to

51
00:02:57,477 --> 00:03:01,214
a magnificent lecture from you
to improve our nurses' mindfulness.

52
00:03:01,281 --> 00:03:02,582
- You!
- Yes?

53
00:03:02,649 --> 00:03:06,653
It sure is a good thing
you didn't get tossed into prison.

54
00:03:08,087 --> 00:03:09,589
Oh, come now.

55
00:03:09,656 --> 00:03:13,059
Those were nothing more than
trumped-up charges.

56
00:03:13,159 --> 00:03:14,727
I wouldn't be so sure.

57
00:03:14,794 --> 00:03:19,399
You have always loved money
more than anything.

58
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:22,769
You frightened me. Anyway, go ahead.

59
00:03:23,036 --> 00:03:24,671
Please approach the podium.

60
00:03:25,138 --> 00:03:27,240
She can talk like that to Director Hiruma?

61
00:03:27,307 --> 00:03:30,009
She started working before he did
at his intern hospital.

62
00:03:30,109 --> 00:03:32,545
Ever since then, he's been meek with her.

63
00:03:32,779 --> 00:03:34,147
The reigning leader of

64
00:03:34,214 --> 00:03:37,417
the Japanese Nursing Confederation,
AKA the Shogun's harem.

65
00:03:37,584 --> 00:03:40,687
Even though she's retired,
she controls the confederation.

66
00:03:40,753 --> 00:03:44,090
Otherwise known as Doctor...

67
00:03:44,424 --> 00:03:46,025
The Reiwa version of Kasuga no Tsubone.

68
00:03:46,092 --> 00:03:47,260
The Reiwa version?

69
00:03:47,527 --> 00:03:49,295
Didn't you just say "doctor"?

70
00:03:49,495 --> 00:03:53,833
Honorary President Mihara,
be gentle with your message.

71
00:03:56,202 --> 00:04:00,139
Those involved in medical care
must be ethical and honest.

72
00:04:00,473 --> 00:04:03,209
There's no place for bribery or collusion!

73
00:04:07,513 --> 00:04:09,449
I want to operate!

74
00:04:09,549 --> 00:04:12,185
<i>Labor reforms are meaningless.</i>

75
00:04:12,619 --> 00:04:14,721
No matter how much the world changes,

76
00:04:14,787 --> 00:04:18,157
that kind of thing
has no place in the medical field.

77
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:20,760
To remain by your patients' side

78
00:04:21,127 --> 00:04:24,264
and to offer even greater
mastery of your skills,

79
00:04:24,364 --> 00:04:27,166
you must work even harder!

80
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:31,471
Do you think you can be a nurse
if you fear death from overworking?

81
00:04:33,373 --> 00:04:35,208
For the patients' sake,

82
00:04:35,308 --> 00:04:38,578
let us work ceaselessly.

83
00:04:42,448 --> 00:04:46,319
This is bad. Who the heck invited her?

84
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,488
Who invited her?

85
00:04:48,588 --> 00:04:50,123
HEAD NURSE
TAMIE SHIRASU

86
00:04:50,223 --> 00:04:51,691
Director Hiruma did.

87
00:04:52,091 --> 00:04:54,127
He can't do this while
Assistant Director Tange is away.

88
00:04:54,193 --> 00:04:57,263
If the Labor Standards Office
finds out, there will be trouble!

89
00:05:00,166 --> 00:05:02,201
Those who work as nurses

90
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:05,371
must be willing to work
themselves to death for patients.

91
00:05:06,506 --> 00:05:08,775
If you're not ready to do that,

92
00:05:09,042 --> 00:05:11,577
then get out this instant!

93
00:05:12,612 --> 00:05:15,515
That's Honorary President Mihara for you.

94
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:19,585
Even in the Reiwa period,
she hasn't changed a bit.

95
00:05:19,652 --> 00:05:20,920
Hold on here.

96
00:05:24,590 --> 00:05:26,793
You are so out of touch with the times!

97
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:29,629
You rude woman! Shame on you!

98
00:05:29,696 --> 00:05:33,166
I'm canceling this lecture!
The lecture is canceled!

99
00:05:33,232 --> 00:05:35,735
Shame on all of you!

100
00:05:36,602 --> 00:05:39,105
Hold on! Stop, all of you!

101
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:44,177
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance
maverick doctor, who was never part of</i>

102
00:05:44,310 --> 00:05:48,214
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

103
00:05:48,648 --> 00:05:50,316
I'm starving.

104
00:05:50,416 --> 00:05:54,253
<i>This woman hates groups, authority,
and restrictions.</i>

105
00:05:54,687 --> 00:05:58,057
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

106
00:05:58,157 --> 00:05:59,659
<i>are her weapons.</i>

107
00:05:59,759 --> 00:06:01,427
I came here because I was invited!

108
00:06:02,261 --> 00:06:04,397
Please wait, Honorary President Mihara.

109
00:06:04,664 --> 00:06:06,499
You don't need to see me off!

110
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:10,036
- You there! Stop!
- What?

111
00:06:11,304 --> 00:06:14,741
- That hurts! What was that for?
- What the heck is that?

112
00:06:15,408 --> 00:06:16,642
What?

113
00:06:17,176 --> 00:06:19,579
How could you put a tattoo on
the healthy skin

114
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:21,547
your parents gave you?

115
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:25,151
Tattoo? It's just a decorative sticker!

116
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:27,320
That's right. A decorative sticker.

117
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:28,521
That hurts!

118
00:06:28,621 --> 00:06:31,023
That's the foolishness of youth!

119
00:06:31,791 --> 00:06:36,529
Tattoos increase the risk of
skin and liver disease.

120
00:06:36,596 --> 00:06:38,264
Don't you understand that?

121
00:06:38,598 --> 00:06:42,235
I've had enough of this bossy lady!
Let's go!

122
00:06:46,572 --> 00:06:48,241
Watch out!

123
00:06:48,641 --> 00:06:50,243
What's with this hospital?

124
00:06:53,813 --> 00:06:55,515
Oh, my.

125
00:06:56,115 --> 00:06:58,017
Allow me to thank you

126
00:06:58,151 --> 00:07:00,253
for saving my grandchild.

127
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,755
You'll be able to see
your great-grandchild too.

128
00:07:03,256 --> 00:07:05,425
You seem like you'll live for a long time.

129
00:07:06,159 --> 00:07:10,596
Thank you so much for caring for
my granddaughter, Nanako, then.

130
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:15,768
Thanks to that,
Nanako has married a foreigner.

131
00:07:16,068 --> 00:07:18,638
She's living happily now in Germany.

132
00:07:18,738 --> 00:07:20,173
Really?

133
00:07:20,506 --> 00:07:23,476
Like you promised me, Dr. Daimon,

134
00:07:23,709 --> 00:07:25,678
my great-grandchild was born.

135
00:07:26,345 --> 00:07:27,413
I'm glad to hear it.

136
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:31,083
Your surgery skills are
quite impressive, Dr. Daimon.

137
00:07:31,184 --> 00:07:33,186
I hear that a lot.

138
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:35,221
Apart from that,

139
00:07:35,321 --> 00:07:38,090
- you still show too much skin!
- That hurts!

140
00:07:38,157 --> 00:07:39,258
- Too much skin!
- That hurts!

141
00:07:39,358 --> 00:07:40,760
- Too much skin!
- Stop that!

142
00:07:41,027 --> 00:07:43,095
What's your problem?
That's ticking me off!

143
00:07:43,196 --> 00:07:46,799
Act more like a doctor
and watch that tongue of yours.

144
00:07:47,099 --> 00:07:48,434
I decline!

145
00:07:52,238 --> 00:07:54,740
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

146
00:07:55,208 --> 00:07:58,544
<i>Otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

147
00:08:27,473 --> 00:08:30,610
Really? You ran into that
Kasuga no Tsubone again?

148
00:08:31,043 --> 00:08:32,144
How is she?

149
00:08:32,545 --> 00:08:35,781
She was just as irritating as ever,

150
00:08:36,582 --> 00:08:38,684
but I don't think she's very well.

151
00:08:38,751 --> 00:08:40,319
Is she sick?

152
00:08:41,254 --> 00:08:42,488
- Too much skin!
- Stop that!

153
00:08:42,655 --> 00:08:45,157
What's your problem?
That's ticking me off!

154
00:08:54,333 --> 00:08:57,169
How long have you had that pain?
Have you been tested?

155
00:08:58,471 --> 00:09:01,474
- Get yourself examined.
- This is none of your business.

156
00:09:02,341 --> 00:09:03,809
Farewell!

157
00:09:08,281 --> 00:09:10,249
<i>She's the boss nurse.</i>

158
00:09:10,316 --> 00:09:12,618
You know she's getting
proper examinations.

159
00:09:12,685 --> 00:09:14,554
I wouldn't be so sure.

160
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:18,057
Anyway, it's ready.

161
00:09:20,326 --> 00:09:22,295
I'll bring us some dishes.

162
00:09:22,361 --> 00:09:24,196
It's that season!

163
00:09:24,497 --> 00:09:26,532
I heard Honorary President Mihara left

164
00:09:26,599 --> 00:09:28,434
because of a commotion.

165
00:09:28,534 --> 00:09:29,735
Yes. Sorry. Goodbye.

166
00:09:30,002 --> 00:09:31,771
- What? Masako.
- Director Kaji, that's no good.

167
00:09:32,071 --> 00:09:33,072
- That's no good.
- What?

168
00:09:33,172 --> 00:09:34,907
Using their first name is
sexual harassment.

169
00:09:34,974 --> 00:09:36,709
- You're kidding. Her name is Masako.
- I'm not.

170
00:09:36,776 --> 00:09:41,013
Due to the labor reforms,
doctors and nurses are actually busier.

171
00:09:41,681 --> 00:09:44,317
What a world we're living in.

172
00:09:45,451 --> 00:09:48,154
Okay, I think I'll go there today.

173
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:49,889
- We're going?
- Yes!

174
00:09:49,956 --> 00:09:51,657
- What place is that?
- Director Ushio

175
00:09:52,024 --> 00:09:55,061
and you too, Murasaki.
How about having a drink with us?

176
00:09:55,127 --> 00:09:56,729
I'm writing a paper.

177
00:09:56,796 --> 00:09:58,364
I'm helping the professor.

178
00:09:59,031 --> 00:10:00,600
It's probably somewhere nasty anyway.

179
00:10:00,666 --> 00:10:02,335
It's "that place," you know.

180
00:10:03,803 --> 00:10:07,039
Director Kaji, count me out too. Sorry.

181
00:10:07,173 --> 00:10:09,342
Director Hiruma asked me
to do a favor for him.

182
00:10:09,408 --> 00:10:12,578
It seems like he still depends on me.
I'll go next time. Sorry.

183
00:10:13,212 --> 00:10:14,180
He was here?

184
00:10:14,347 --> 00:10:17,617
We will now begin a
pancreaticoduodenectomy.

185
00:10:17,817 --> 00:10:19,485
- Let's begin.
- Let's begin.

186
00:10:19,585 --> 00:10:21,587
Get us some tacos! Hit the nurse button!

187
00:10:21,721 --> 00:10:23,122
Hurry up and get her!

188
00:10:23,322 --> 00:10:26,359
- Yes?
- Meg! There you are!

189
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:28,160
I'm exhausted!

190
00:10:28,227 --> 00:10:30,396
Shoot me full of a nice strong shot!

191
00:10:30,463 --> 00:10:32,031
Sure thing! Okay!

192
00:10:32,131 --> 00:10:34,367
Here comes your shot!

193
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:36,836
- This will hurt.
- That hurts!

194
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:39,105
- This will hurt.
- It's making me swell!

195
00:10:39,205 --> 00:10:40,673
This is an emergency!

196
00:10:40,773 --> 00:10:43,509
- Metzenbaum scissors!
- Metzenbaum scissors!

197
00:10:43,676 --> 00:10:46,178
You can call them by their
first names here, and they're so kind.

198
00:10:46,245 --> 00:10:47,413
You're so right!

199
00:10:48,481 --> 00:10:49,949
Welcome!

200
00:10:50,683 --> 00:10:51,717
Let me introduce you.

201
00:10:51,784 --> 00:10:55,521
- This is a newbie, Masa.
- It's nice to meet you!

202
00:10:56,622 --> 00:10:59,692
- You're Ms. Ohma!
- Here, I'm Masa.

203
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:02,328
That's not the problem.
If the hospital finds out--

204
00:11:02,395 --> 00:11:04,163
Illicit business? That's just wrong!

205
00:11:04,263 --> 00:11:05,498
I know that,

206
00:11:05,598 --> 00:11:08,567
but the hospital won't let me
do enough night shifts or overtime.

207
00:11:08,934 --> 00:11:11,637
I want to work more
so I can send money back home.

208
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:14,907
Okay, Director!
It's time to take your blood pressure!

209
00:11:14,974 --> 00:11:18,077
How can I get excited... Please, do it!

210
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:21,947
We're here!

211
00:11:24,083 --> 00:11:26,752
Rika, I've come back.

212
00:11:26,819 --> 00:11:29,055
Welcome, Usshi and Murarin!

213
00:11:29,121 --> 00:11:32,158
- That nurse cap of yours is cute!
- Thank you.

214
00:11:32,224 --> 00:11:34,960
Rika, the usual, watered down.

215
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:36,829
- Watered down?
- It's too strong lately.

216
00:11:37,063 --> 00:11:39,799
Murarin! Are you done with your paper?

217
00:11:43,836 --> 00:11:45,137
Good evening!

218
00:11:45,471 --> 00:11:48,207
He said his usual is too strong.

219
00:11:48,307 --> 00:11:49,842
They're obviously regulars.

220
00:11:51,377 --> 00:11:52,845
I totally get it!

221
00:11:54,814 --> 00:11:57,249
I am terribly sorry.

222
00:11:58,317 --> 00:12:01,287
You accepted our invitation
to speak, but then that happened,

223
00:12:02,021 --> 00:12:03,723
so I can understand why you're upset.

224
00:12:04,023 --> 00:12:05,391
I am truly sorry.

225
00:12:06,692 --> 00:12:09,995
I have this for you.

226
00:12:10,162 --> 00:12:14,133
This is a small token of apology
from Director Hiruma.

227
00:12:14,500 --> 00:12:16,202
MASAE'S SON
GORO MIHARA

228
00:12:16,302 --> 00:12:18,237
Mom, please forgive them.

229
00:12:19,271 --> 00:12:21,807
- Thank you so much for coming.
- It's no problem at all.

230
00:12:24,343 --> 00:12:26,045
Shinnosuke!

231
00:12:26,712 --> 00:12:28,380
Shiro, here's a snack!

232
00:12:30,015 --> 00:12:32,051
Stop that, Shinnosuke!

233
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:35,187
- All right now.
- Such a sweet grandson.

234
00:12:35,287 --> 00:12:37,356
- He's my great-grandson.
- Oh, I see.

235
00:12:37,456 --> 00:12:40,126
Shinnosuke, give that to your grandfather.

236
00:12:40,226 --> 00:12:41,393
Fine.

237
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:43,329
Thank you.

238
00:12:43,796 --> 00:12:45,397
Shinnosuke!

239
00:12:46,198 --> 00:12:49,034
Darn you! Quit wiggling your bottom!

240
00:12:49,301 --> 00:12:50,336
Shinnosuke!

241
00:12:50,402 --> 00:12:52,138
- I'm sorry about that.
- It's all right.

242
00:12:54,774 --> 00:12:56,575
Open it up.

243
00:12:59,779 --> 00:13:01,647
- Look under that too.
- What?

244
00:13:04,183 --> 00:13:06,018
- Under that too!
- What?

245
00:13:12,024 --> 00:13:13,793
I despise bribery!

246
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:15,494
You've got it wrong.

247
00:13:15,561 --> 00:13:17,997
That's the lecture fee
we couldn't give you today.

248
00:13:18,097 --> 00:13:20,599
I know Director Hiruma's intentions
perfectly well.

249
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:23,302
He wants me to support him in
the election for chairman

250
00:13:23,369 --> 00:13:25,171
of the Japan Physicians Club.

251
00:13:26,172 --> 00:13:28,674
By all means, give him your support!

252
00:13:30,509 --> 00:13:34,079
Take this wretched thing back with you!

253
00:13:36,348 --> 00:13:37,817
- Mom!
- Mrs. Mihara!

254
00:13:38,083 --> 00:13:39,518
- Grandma, are you okay?
- Mom!

255
00:13:39,618 --> 00:13:40,820
What should we do?

256
00:13:40,986 --> 00:13:42,855
At any rate, bring her to our hospital!

257
00:13:42,922 --> 00:13:45,825
- I'm not going to any hospital.
- Don't be ridiculous, Mom!

258
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:48,093
- Hana, let's get a dog.
- What?

259
00:13:48,227 --> 00:13:49,829
- I want a dog.
- Later.

260
00:13:50,095 --> 00:13:52,031
My! I like this!

261
00:13:53,465 --> 00:13:56,735
TAKASHI EBINA

262
00:13:58,637 --> 00:14:00,773
Why are you calling at this hour, Ebina?

263
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,542
She just collapsed at her home,
so we brought her to our hospital.

264
00:14:04,376 --> 00:14:05,711
Mrs. Mihara?

265
00:14:06,779 --> 00:14:08,480
Darling!

266
00:14:11,684 --> 00:14:15,521
Ebina, are you listening? You know that

267
00:14:15,588 --> 00:14:19,758
the election for chairman of
Japan Physicians Club is coming up.

268
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:25,030
Do whatever it takes
to cure President Mihara,

269
00:14:25,130 --> 00:14:28,267
the leader of 1.5 million nurses,

270
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:31,103
at Totei University Hospital. Understood?

271
00:14:31,170 --> 00:14:33,739
I understand. We'll do whatever it takes
to cure her here.

272
00:14:33,806 --> 00:14:37,009
I'll have her thoroughly examined
right away. Goodbye.

273
00:14:37,743 --> 00:14:39,778
Do not examine me.

274
00:14:41,113 --> 00:14:42,114
Mom!

275
00:14:42,648 --> 00:14:45,217
I will not allow you to examine me.

276
00:14:46,452 --> 00:14:47,686
How can you say that?

277
00:14:47,820 --> 00:14:49,955
If you're going to examine me,

278
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,524
I'm leaving.

279
00:14:53,125 --> 00:14:54,460
Mom!

280
00:14:57,029 --> 00:14:58,097
OPERATING ROOM

281
00:14:59,431 --> 00:15:00,766
This feels so nice!

282
00:15:01,367 --> 00:15:02,768
I could do five more!

283
00:15:02,868 --> 00:15:04,770
Nobody else needs surgery today.

284
00:15:05,037 --> 00:15:06,205
Really?

285
00:15:06,705 --> 00:15:09,341
Say, are you sure there's nothing
wrong with you?

286
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:12,044
- Cut that out!
- I'll operate if there is!

287
00:15:12,111 --> 00:15:14,179
- What's your problem?
- You sure are skinny.

288
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:17,483
Dr. Daimon!

289
00:15:19,118 --> 00:15:21,353
- Come with me.
- What?

290
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:25,491
- What's going on?
- Since she owes you for

291
00:15:25,624 --> 00:15:27,593
what you did for her granddaughter,

292
00:15:27,693 --> 00:15:30,396
Honorary President Mihara is
sure to listen to you.

293
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:33,265
I should probably go too.

294
00:15:33,565 --> 00:15:35,267
Here you are.

295
00:15:35,334 --> 00:15:36,669
Are you a new nurse?

296
00:15:37,736 --> 00:15:38,704
Yes.

297
00:15:39,204 --> 00:15:41,006
Even when you serve a tray,

298
00:15:41,173 --> 00:15:45,110
put yourself in the patient's shoes.
Instead of like this,

299
00:15:45,744 --> 00:15:47,346
serve it like this.

300
00:15:47,746 --> 00:15:50,616
Thank you. That's very helpful.

301
00:15:51,517 --> 00:15:54,119
Your lecture yesterday was
truly inspiring.

302
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:57,823
To me, you are the ideal nurse,
Honorary President Mihara.

303
00:15:59,491 --> 00:16:01,593
You're a rare girl in this era.

304
00:16:01,727 --> 00:16:03,395
Thank you.

305
00:16:05,497 --> 00:16:06,598
Excuse us.

306
00:16:06,699 --> 00:16:09,401
If we can't examine you,
we can't operate on you or treat you.

307
00:16:09,535 --> 00:16:11,136
Let's get you examined right away.

308
00:16:12,104 --> 00:16:13,138
Excuse me.

309
00:16:13,205 --> 00:16:15,074
- Don't touch me!
- Sorry.

310
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:16,642
- Take her.
- Yes, ma'am.

311
00:16:17,209 --> 00:16:19,745
I'm sorry. These are Dr. Daimon's orders.

312
00:16:20,045 --> 00:16:22,581
If you lay a finger on me, I'll sue!

313
00:16:22,748 --> 00:16:23,582
I'm sorry!

314
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:27,720
What's wrong?
Getting examined isn't going to hurt you.

315
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:37,629
There must be something
that you don't want anyone to see.

316
00:16:38,130 --> 00:16:41,200
- Don't be ridiculous.
- I've had a ton of experience,

317
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:43,202
so no body will surprise me.

318
00:16:44,103 --> 00:16:48,107
Even if you've got two hearts
or your blood is thick as black mud.

319
00:16:48,207 --> 00:16:50,676
- My blood is perfectly clean!
- I wouldn't be so sure.

320
00:16:50,776 --> 00:16:52,811
- What a rude woman.
- Same to you.

321
00:16:55,214 --> 00:16:56,882
Fine.

322
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:01,487
But I'll only allow you to test my blood.

323
00:17:06,158 --> 00:17:09,161
- Just thrust it in!
- Yes, ma'am.

324
00:17:09,228 --> 00:17:11,497
Come on. Just a blood test?

325
00:17:11,563 --> 00:17:15,100
- Give her a CT and MRI as well.
- Okay.

326
00:17:15,167 --> 00:17:17,503
- I decline!
- Okay. Sorry.

327
00:17:19,405 --> 00:17:20,506
Hurry it up!

328
00:17:20,572 --> 00:17:23,142
- Hurry up and do it.
- No way! It's impossible.

329
00:17:25,310 --> 00:17:27,613
This week's pre-op conference
will now commence.

330
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:30,449
The first case is a VIP among VIPs.

331
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:33,652
Masae Mihara, age 73,

332
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:36,422
the Honorary President of
the Japanese Nursing Confederation.

333
00:17:36,989 --> 00:17:39,558
However, she's refusing to be examined,

334
00:17:39,625 --> 00:17:42,428
so this is the only data we have on her.

335
00:17:43,362 --> 00:17:45,297
Judging from the pain in her right chest

336
00:17:45,364 --> 00:17:47,232
and the elevated inflammatory response,

337
00:17:47,433 --> 00:17:49,435
she most likely has shingles.

338
00:17:49,501 --> 00:17:52,771
No, it's also possible
she has polymyalgia.

339
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:54,039
Objection!

340
00:17:54,473 --> 00:17:57,676
She has numbness in her back
and an ache in her right chest.

341
00:17:58,177 --> 00:18:00,679
Therefore, I believe she has
dumbbell neurinoma.

342
00:18:01,013 --> 00:18:04,216
If it's not operated on immediately,
she's in danger. Let me do it.

343
00:18:04,316 --> 00:18:07,086
How can you possibly be so certain?

344
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,389
- My intuition.
- "Intuition"?

345
00:18:10,489 --> 00:18:13,192
Just your intuition?
Then you're just guessing.

346
00:18:13,325 --> 00:18:15,327
Quit acting like you're so right.

347
00:18:15,727 --> 00:18:17,663
What does the AI say?

348
00:18:18,130 --> 00:18:22,134
There's so little examination data,
she cannot make a diagnosis.

349
00:18:22,301 --> 00:18:23,769
It figures.

350
00:18:24,303 --> 00:18:27,139
Let's consider administering
steroids and PPI.

351
00:18:27,473 --> 00:18:28,607
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

352
00:18:28,707 --> 00:18:29,608
Excuse me!

353
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:34,546
I got Honorary President Mihara's
secret CT scans!

354
00:18:35,013 --> 00:18:36,315
- Really?
- Yes.

355
00:18:36,381 --> 00:18:38,283
It was at a private clinic,

356
00:18:38,350 --> 00:18:41,186
but her son remembered she had
a CT scan done there six months ago.

357
00:18:41,386 --> 00:18:43,055
Hey, Daimon! No cheating!

358
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:49,428
What?

359
00:18:50,095 --> 00:18:53,198
She has a dumbbell-shaped tumor
on her TH9.

360
00:18:53,465 --> 00:18:55,534
That's dumbbell neurinoma.

361
00:18:55,601 --> 00:18:56,768
See, I told you.

362
00:18:57,002 --> 00:18:58,170
Told us what?

363
00:18:58,270 --> 00:19:00,372
How did Dr. Daimon know
without seeing her scans?

364
00:19:00,506 --> 00:19:02,107
I see it a lot during her surgeries.

365
00:19:02,207 --> 00:19:04,376
She has her own special animal instinct.

366
00:19:04,443 --> 00:19:07,546
I see. Her special skill
and hobby is surgery, after all.

367
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:12,317
If she's not operated on right away,
her back pain will grow even worse.

368
00:19:13,051 --> 00:19:16,054
If nothing is done,
it'll apply pressure to the spinal cord

369
00:19:16,255 --> 00:19:18,423
and could even cause paralysis
in her legs.

370
00:19:18,557 --> 00:19:20,659
That's why you need to let me operate.

371
00:19:20,726 --> 00:19:23,295
Can we let a part-timer operate on a VIP?

372
00:19:23,395 --> 00:19:24,363
Certainly not.

373
00:19:24,429 --> 00:19:28,000
As director of Next-Generation
Intelligent Surgery, I will operate.

374
00:19:28,066 --> 00:19:31,737
I will use the primary approach,
from the back

375
00:19:32,271 --> 00:19:34,473
and make a 20-centimeter incision
down her spine.

376
00:19:35,073 --> 00:19:37,476
I'll extract the tumor via laminectomy.

377
00:19:37,609 --> 00:19:40,179
That will cause excessive
post-op stress on the patient.

378
00:19:40,646 --> 00:19:42,347
I will perform it via thoracoscope.

379
00:19:42,781 --> 00:19:45,417
I will approach via thoracoscope,
detach the tumor,

380
00:19:45,517 --> 00:19:48,420
then excise the tumor through her back

381
00:19:48,554 --> 00:19:50,556
without cutting into the vertebral arch.

382
00:19:50,789 --> 00:19:51,690
I see.

383
00:19:51,757 --> 00:19:55,194
Objection! This image is six months old.

384
00:19:55,294 --> 00:19:56,762
It's sure to have progressed further.

385
00:19:57,095 --> 00:20:00,532
The best way is to open her up from
the back and decide how to proceed.

386
00:20:00,699 --> 00:20:02,401
You're always like that!

387
00:20:02,467 --> 00:20:04,203
You're so haphazard, you and never plan!

388
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,606
We'll never decide anything at this rate.

389
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:10,609
This is a pretty important VIP.

390
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:14,213
Let's decide after consulting with
the hospital director. Okay?

391
00:20:16,348 --> 00:20:19,218
Really? It's that serious?

392
00:20:19,284 --> 00:20:20,786
If it progresses rapidly,

393
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:23,355
it could become
quite a difficult operation.

394
00:20:23,422 --> 00:20:25,424
- According to--
- According to the AI's analysis,

395
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:29,361
there is a 34 percent chance of
post-op paralysis.

396
00:20:29,428 --> 00:20:30,762
Thirty-four percent?

397
00:20:31,330 --> 00:20:32,831
That's risky.

398
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:35,167
Well then,

399
00:20:35,534 --> 00:20:38,170
there's no need for us
to run that kind of risk.

400
00:20:38,270 --> 00:20:39,571
Hold on a second!

401
00:20:39,671 --> 00:20:42,441
You're the one who said
to cure her no matter what!

402
00:20:42,774 --> 00:20:44,543
- Did I say that?
- Yes, you did!

403
00:20:45,711 --> 00:20:46,812
Did I?

404
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:50,382
No. Sorry.

405
00:20:51,283 --> 00:20:54,319
We'll have to transfer
Honorary President Mihara

406
00:20:54,486 --> 00:20:57,155
to another hospital, I'm afraid.

407
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:58,590
You must be kidding!

408
00:20:58,790 --> 00:21:00,492
You want her to die at another hospital?

409
00:21:01,226 --> 00:21:03,595
- You call yourself a doctor?
- What?

410
00:21:06,798 --> 00:21:07,899
That scared me.

411
00:21:07,966 --> 00:21:09,201
Didn't Nichotan

412
00:21:09,334 --> 00:21:13,238
send me a love letter from Paris,
saying I could operate all I want?

413
00:21:13,305 --> 00:21:14,339
MESSAGE FOR DR. DAIMON

414
00:21:14,406 --> 00:21:15,941
WITH LOVE FROM PARIS,
NICHOLAS TANGE

415
00:21:16,008 --> 00:21:17,442
Daimon!

416
00:21:18,377 --> 00:21:22,080
I am the hospital director, you know.

417
00:21:22,347 --> 00:21:25,217
I have the final say in this!

418
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:27,519
Getting upset increases
your blood pressure.

419
00:21:27,586 --> 00:21:28,754
Oh, right.

420
00:21:28,820 --> 00:21:32,658
As for surgery, I think it's impossible.

421
00:21:33,492 --> 00:21:34,660
What do you mean?

422
00:21:34,826 --> 00:21:36,428
Honorary President Mihara says

423
00:21:36,495 --> 00:21:38,597
she'll never let her back be cut open.

424
00:21:38,697 --> 00:21:41,266
Operating through her back is
the only way!

425
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:42,668
The AI says so too.

426
00:21:42,734 --> 00:21:45,470
She said she absolutely refuses
to let that happen.

427
00:21:47,739 --> 00:21:49,207
Then

428
00:21:49,341 --> 00:21:51,410
we don't have a choice, do we?

429
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:58,583
Mom, please let them operate.

430
00:22:00,285 --> 00:22:02,654
Why can't they operate on you
through your back?

431
00:22:03,221 --> 00:22:05,657
I'd be lying face down
on the operating table.

432
00:22:06,024 --> 00:22:07,292
That's right.

433
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:09,995
Like this, right?

434
00:22:10,662 --> 00:22:14,232
Cut that out. I could never turn
my rear toward the surgeons

435
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:18,236
and nurses operating on me.

436
00:22:18,303 --> 00:22:21,506
What are you talking about?
This is a matter of life and death.

437
00:22:21,606 --> 00:22:23,275
Grandma.

438
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:36,054
PRIVATE ROOM B

439
00:22:37,956 --> 00:22:39,858
KANBARA FAMOUS DOCTOR AGENCY

440
00:22:40,826 --> 00:22:43,362
She can't turn her rear toward
the surgeon?

441
00:22:43,462 --> 00:22:45,097
Now that's an old-fashioned woman.

442
00:22:45,163 --> 00:22:47,132
It sure is. It makes no sense.

443
00:22:47,265 --> 00:22:50,802
It sure is frustrating.
I'd like her to live even longer.

444
00:22:51,203 --> 00:22:54,339
She's a ray of hope for us single mothers.

445
00:22:54,406 --> 00:22:55,607
You look up to her, Hiromi?

446
00:22:55,707 --> 00:22:58,377
That's right. I may have been divorced,

447
00:22:58,443 --> 00:23:01,113
but Kasuga no Tsubone is
the original unwed mother.

448
00:23:01,179 --> 00:23:02,714
Really? I didn't know that.

449
00:23:03,048 --> 00:23:06,651
She gave birth to a boy without
telling anyone who the father is.

450
00:23:06,785 --> 00:23:09,421
Akira, you sure know a lot.

451
00:23:09,521 --> 00:23:11,089
There were a lot of rumors back then.

452
00:23:11,189 --> 00:23:14,559
A big politician was hospitalized
at Totei University at that time,

453
00:23:14,659 --> 00:23:17,295
so there were rumors
that he was the father,

454
00:23:17,396 --> 00:23:19,564
or maybe a young intern.

455
00:23:19,664 --> 00:23:21,366
What's the truth?

456
00:23:21,466 --> 00:23:23,702
I don't know what the real truth is.

457
00:23:23,802 --> 00:23:28,340
Women carry some secrets to their grave.

458
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:31,343
I doubt Michiko has any.

459
00:23:31,410 --> 00:23:32,511
You're right.

460
00:23:32,577 --> 00:23:33,712
It's your turn.

461
00:23:33,812 --> 00:23:35,814
Then what about you, Akira?

462
00:23:37,516 --> 00:23:38,750
Why are you acting like that?

463
00:23:41,353 --> 00:23:43,688
Come to think of it,
what happened to Rat Coin?

464
00:23:43,789 --> 00:23:46,091
Why don't you tell me how much we've made?

465
00:23:46,525 --> 00:23:48,059
Michiko, I'm sorry.

466
00:23:48,326 --> 00:23:51,196
They went bankrupt without any reason.

467
00:23:51,363 --> 00:23:52,397
Bankrupt?

468
00:23:52,464 --> 00:23:53,832
They're worth zero.

469
00:23:54,099 --> 00:23:56,067
I knew it!

470
00:23:57,369 --> 00:23:59,204
What about our shining white mansion?

471
00:23:59,571 --> 00:24:02,441
I'm sorry. It's all gone.

472
00:24:02,707 --> 00:24:05,710
Are you kidding? Darn it!

473
00:24:05,977 --> 00:24:07,479
I have to apologize once more.

474
00:24:07,679 --> 00:24:10,782
That gives me <i>ron</i>. Thirteen orphans.

475
00:24:13,485 --> 00:24:16,221
Gosh, darn you!

476
00:24:16,288 --> 00:24:17,456
Don't cry!

477
00:24:18,723 --> 00:24:21,126
Honorary President Mihara will

478
00:24:21,426 --> 00:24:23,528
check out of the hospital today.

479
00:24:24,629 --> 00:24:25,597
I see.

480
00:24:26,598 --> 00:24:28,099
That's good for us.

481
00:24:28,733 --> 00:24:32,204
We can't let the leader
of all the nurses die

482
00:24:32,804 --> 00:24:34,573
at Totei University Hospital.

483
00:24:36,007 --> 00:24:38,777
- Goodbye.
- Bye. Thank you for reporting.

484
00:24:39,044 --> 00:24:42,280
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

485
00:24:42,347 --> 00:24:43,548
She's checking out.

486
00:24:43,615 --> 00:24:45,417
SECRETARY TO THE HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
RURI IKURA

487
00:24:45,617 --> 00:24:48,420
Is that right? You're from Aomori as well?

488
00:24:48,553 --> 00:24:50,822
My little brothers are still very young.

489
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:54,359
You must have to earn a lot
to send back to your family.

490
00:24:54,459 --> 00:24:57,062
That's right. I have to earn a lot.

491
00:24:57,128 --> 00:24:59,164
Money is very important.

492
00:24:59,464 --> 00:25:01,600
But more important than anything is

493
00:25:01,666 --> 00:25:05,604
understanding the pain and suffering
that patients go through.

494
00:25:05,704 --> 00:25:06,671
That's right.

495
00:25:06,738 --> 00:25:08,206
Then

496
00:25:08,707 --> 00:25:12,244
why don't you try to understand
the suffering of the patient's family?

497
00:25:14,613 --> 00:25:16,381
An operation will cure you.

498
00:25:16,448 --> 00:25:18,316
I told you to butt out, didn't I?

499
00:25:18,383 --> 00:25:20,218
If you check out now, you'll die!

500
00:25:20,285 --> 00:25:21,753
That's what I want!

501
00:25:23,221 --> 00:25:24,589
Mrs. Mihara...

502
00:25:24,756 --> 00:25:28,193
I am going to change now, so please leave.

503
00:25:28,593 --> 00:25:30,996
- I will assist you.
- No, thank you!

504
00:25:32,297 --> 00:25:33,632
Get out of the way!

505
00:25:35,534 --> 00:25:37,102
Goodbye.

506
00:25:38,136 --> 00:25:39,604
We'll talk when we get home.

507
00:25:40,138 --> 00:25:44,042
Doctor, I'm terribly sorry for
all the trouble we've caused.

508
00:25:45,810 --> 00:25:49,247
Once Mom makes up her mind,
she won't budge.

509
00:25:50,115 --> 00:25:52,384
She raised me all by herself,

510
00:25:52,450 --> 00:25:54,819
so there's nothing I can do to defy her.

511
00:26:11,002 --> 00:26:13,004
She's kind to her grandchildren
and great-grandchildren,

512
00:26:13,138 --> 00:26:15,407
but she's really quite stubborn.

513
00:26:15,774 --> 00:26:17,208
Isn't that right?

514
00:26:17,609 --> 00:26:19,611
Even when we went to
a hot spring together,

515
00:26:19,711 --> 00:26:22,414
she never took a bath with the rest of us.

516
00:26:23,081 --> 00:26:24,082
Why not?

517
00:26:24,182 --> 00:26:28,153
She says a woman cannot show
her flesh to others.

518
00:26:31,423 --> 00:26:33,592
She's taking long. I'll go check on her.

519
00:26:39,598 --> 00:26:42,167
Mom? Have you changed?

520
00:26:42,701 --> 00:26:44,102
I'm coming in.

521
00:26:44,769 --> 00:26:46,171
Mom, we're...

522
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:48,707
Mom?

523
00:26:49,207 --> 00:26:50,475
Mom!

524
00:26:52,177 --> 00:26:53,511
Mom!

525
00:26:54,746 --> 00:26:56,114
Hold on!

526
00:26:56,247 --> 00:26:58,783
Doctor! Blood! Mom...

527
00:26:59,050 --> 00:27:00,518
Mom spat blood out!

528
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:04,189
- Are you all right?
- Mrs. Mihara!

529
00:27:04,289 --> 00:27:05,457
- Mom!
- Grandma!

530
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:07,325
Mom!

531
00:27:07,425 --> 00:27:09,527
She's vomiting blood from
the upper digestive tract bleeding.

532
00:27:09,594 --> 00:27:10,562
Endoscope immediately!

533
00:27:10,695 --> 00:27:11,596
Yes, ma'am!

534
00:27:12,063 --> 00:27:13,665
- Mom!
- Grandma!

535
00:27:25,276 --> 00:27:26,578
Daimon,

536
00:27:27,012 --> 00:27:30,649
you don't intend to operate on her
before she wakes up, do you?

537
00:27:32,417 --> 00:27:35,453
Don't do anything crazy.
The director wants her out.

538
00:27:38,757 --> 00:27:41,259
She gets an MRI next, right?
It's free now.

539
00:27:41,393 --> 00:27:43,395
- You're in on this too?
- I'll get it ready.

540
00:27:43,762 --> 00:27:46,297
Wait. We're not taking an MRI.

541
00:27:46,364 --> 00:27:47,365
What?

542
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:50,301
- Aren't you going to operate?
- This is all we're doing.

543
00:27:52,804 --> 00:27:54,105
Thank goodness.

544
00:28:11,056 --> 00:28:15,593
I figured out why you refuse to
have tests or get examined.

545
00:28:17,128 --> 00:28:19,264
You saw it, did you?

546
00:28:19,731 --> 00:28:21,566
My secret.

547
00:28:23,401 --> 00:28:27,572
We didn't take an MRI
since it could cause burns.

548
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:32,544
This is the one thing
I will risk my life to save.

549
00:28:35,113 --> 00:28:38,683
Can you promise not to tell my son
or anyone else?

550
00:28:48,426 --> 00:28:49,794
I promise.

551
00:28:52,764 --> 00:28:54,365
Allow me to operate.

552
00:28:55,800 --> 00:28:57,669
I told you, no operations.

553
00:28:57,769 --> 00:29:00,071
I will protect what's precious to you.

554
00:29:00,505 --> 00:29:02,140
I won't damage even a millimeter.

555
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:07,512
This is a promise between women.

556
00:29:11,082 --> 00:29:12,817
Dr. Daimon...

557
00:29:16,087 --> 00:29:19,057
I never fail.

558
00:29:36,007 --> 00:29:38,977
- Dang, I'm tired.
- The patient is the most tired.

559
00:29:39,577 --> 00:29:41,479
How unusual!
You're still here, Dr. Daimon.

560
00:29:41,579 --> 00:29:43,681
Really? It's way past quitting time too.

561
00:29:55,126 --> 00:29:57,295
- Good night.
- Daimon,

562
00:29:57,428 --> 00:29:59,597
you decided not to operate
thanks to my advice, right?

563
00:30:01,766 --> 00:30:03,635
Thank you, Daimon.

564
00:30:04,569 --> 00:30:07,806
You know, looking at how far we've come,

565
00:30:08,072 --> 00:30:12,076
we sure did spend a heck of
a lot of money on this system.

566
00:30:13,411 --> 00:30:16,648
This button controls the surgical lamps
in operating room one.

567
00:30:16,748 --> 00:30:18,683
- I see.
- Like this.

568
00:30:19,117 --> 00:30:20,618
Oh, they turned off.

569
00:30:20,685 --> 00:30:22,387
That's interesting.

570
00:30:22,754 --> 00:30:25,557
Turn on. Turn off.

571
00:30:25,657 --> 00:30:28,660
It's turned on. It's turned off.

572
00:30:28,726 --> 00:30:31,462
Once it's on, turn it off.

573
00:30:31,729 --> 00:30:33,665
I wish he would leave soon.

574
00:30:34,065 --> 00:30:36,134
- It's turned off.
- Director!

575
00:30:36,201 --> 00:30:38,670
You're so busy,
you forgot your wedding anniversary.

576
00:30:38,770 --> 00:30:40,338
Oh, that's right!

577
00:30:42,307 --> 00:30:46,211
Your wife has been getting into
social media lately,

578
00:30:46,311 --> 00:30:49,180
so I made reservations for you
at a photo-worthy restaurant.

579
00:30:49,247 --> 00:30:50,648
- You did, Head Nurse?
- That's right.

580
00:30:50,748 --> 00:30:53,084
I'm sorry for being so forward.

581
00:30:53,184 --> 00:30:56,154
No, that's all right.
Thank you for your concern.

582
00:30:56,421 --> 00:31:00,291
Well, I see.
Then I guess I have no choice but to go.

583
00:31:00,458 --> 00:31:03,428
- Yes, it's time.
- I see. Then I'll...

584
00:31:08,399 --> 00:31:10,068
Sorry to call you here suddenly.

585
00:31:10,134 --> 00:31:12,570
Top-secret surgery. How exhilarating!

586
00:31:18,042 --> 00:31:20,745
I will do my very best.
I look forward to working with you.

587
00:31:20,812 --> 00:31:23,615
This newbie is the instrument nurse?
That's a promotion.

588
00:31:23,681 --> 00:31:24,849
Thank you.

589
00:31:25,283 --> 00:31:27,518
The patient asked for her.
I had no choice.

590
00:31:28,319 --> 00:31:31,089
So where are the first
and second assistants?

591
00:31:31,322 --> 00:31:32,523
There aren't any.

592
00:31:32,724 --> 00:31:35,193
- You mean it's just us three?
- That's right.

593
00:31:35,793 --> 00:31:38,363
Well, I guess it's not impossible.

594
00:31:46,804 --> 00:31:49,841
BP, 104 over 70. Pulse, 80.

595
00:31:50,108 --> 00:31:51,776
- Let's begin.
- Wait.

596
00:31:51,843 --> 00:31:53,278
She's not prone.

597
00:31:53,344 --> 00:31:55,079
I'm approaching from her side.

598
00:31:55,313 --> 00:31:57,215
- Scalpel.
- Right.

599
00:32:08,793 --> 00:32:10,728
Did they forget to shut things down?

600
00:32:10,795 --> 00:32:12,497
What a waste.

601
00:32:12,697 --> 00:32:14,632
We need to reduce expenditures.

602
00:32:20,238 --> 00:32:21,406
What is she doing?

603
00:32:23,641 --> 00:32:24,876
Wait!

604
00:32:34,352 --> 00:32:36,120
Let me through.

605
00:32:36,220 --> 00:32:37,355
We refuse!

606
00:32:38,056 --> 00:32:39,624
- We refuse!
- We refuse!

607
00:32:41,159 --> 00:32:43,461
OPERATING ROOM

608
00:32:43,561 --> 00:32:46,698
I can hardly believe
you remembered our anniversary.

609
00:32:47,231 --> 00:32:50,234
And even at a restaurant
that I liked online.

610
00:32:50,335 --> 00:32:52,537
This is so Instagrammable!

611
00:32:53,204 --> 00:32:56,307
What? They charge double the asking price?

612
00:32:56,774 --> 00:32:58,476
- Whatever.
- Hold on.

613
00:32:58,810 --> 00:33:00,411
Can you take a photo of us?

614
00:33:00,712 --> 00:33:01,779
Certainly.

615
00:33:02,547 --> 00:33:03,581
Thank you.

616
00:33:03,715 --> 00:33:07,719
Are you going to post this
to show off to all your friends?

617
00:33:07,785 --> 00:33:11,723
<i>I need to increase my followers
by showing how happy I am.</i>

618
00:33:12,223 --> 00:33:15,193
<i>Can't we enjoy our happiness alone,
just the two of us?</i>

619
00:33:15,259 --> 00:33:17,528
<i>Don't look so sullen. Smile.</i>

620
00:33:19,397 --> 00:33:21,532
<i>I'm getting a call.</i>

621
00:33:22,266 --> 00:33:24,002
<i>It's from Mari Hamachi.</i>

622
00:33:24,469 --> 00:33:26,137
<i>Yes, Hamachi? What is it?</i>

623
00:33:26,270 --> 00:33:28,506
<i>- Here goes.
- Wait! Hold on!</i>

624
00:33:31,376 --> 00:33:34,545
There's trouble! Ms. Daimon has
taken over an operating room

625
00:33:34,645 --> 00:33:36,214
and is operating without permission!

626
00:33:36,547 --> 00:33:38,449
She's operating on
Honorary President Mihara!

627
00:33:39,150 --> 00:33:40,685
Are you kidding me?

628
00:33:52,463 --> 00:33:55,366
Instrument nurse, get across from me.

629
00:33:55,767 --> 00:33:58,269
- Hurry up.
- Yes, ma'am.

630
00:34:02,774 --> 00:34:04,442
- Suction.
- Right.

631
00:34:05,076 --> 00:34:06,511
- Hurry up.
- Right.

632
00:34:07,412 --> 00:34:08,646
Excuse me.

633
00:34:15,119 --> 00:34:17,622
The tumor is blocking my view
of the nerve root.

634
00:34:18,122 --> 00:34:21,192
If the nerve root is damaged,
she'll become disabled.

635
00:34:21,492 --> 00:34:24,128
Shouldn't you approach from the back?

636
00:34:49,420 --> 00:34:51,422
So this is what's up.

637
00:34:51,489 --> 00:34:53,458
No wonder it's a top-secret surgery

638
00:34:53,724 --> 00:34:56,194
and you're operating
from the side instead of the back.

639
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:58,629
I made a promise, woman to woman.

640
00:35:04,769 --> 00:35:07,371
I'll carefully remove the tumor.

641
00:35:07,605 --> 00:35:09,107
- Metzenbaum scissors.
- Here.

642
00:35:18,249 --> 00:35:19,684
Mrs. Mihara!

643
00:35:21,752 --> 00:35:24,555
- Where is Mrs. Mihara?
- This way. Follow me.

644
00:35:26,424 --> 00:35:28,226
Hana! Wait!

645
00:35:28,459 --> 00:35:30,628
Ms. Hamachi! You're going too fast!

646
00:35:32,663 --> 00:35:33,731
Daimon!

647
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,099
Daimon!

648
00:35:35,166 --> 00:35:39,170
What the heck do you think
you're doing, you fool?

649
00:35:40,171 --> 00:35:43,274
<i>Stop operating immediately! Daimon!</i>

650
00:35:43,341 --> 00:35:46,144
It's that troublesome
raccoon of an old man.

651
00:35:46,277 --> 00:35:49,080
Listen! What you're doing now is

652
00:35:50,214 --> 00:35:52,183
clearly illegal!

653
00:35:52,316 --> 00:35:54,352
<i>It's illegal! I'll sue you!</i>

654
00:35:54,418 --> 00:35:56,587
If I stop now, the patient will die.

655
00:35:56,721 --> 00:35:59,490
No! Don't you dare do that!

656
00:35:59,624 --> 00:36:01,425
Make the operation a success!

657
00:36:01,492 --> 00:36:02,994
Please!

658
00:36:04,629 --> 00:36:09,767
Daimon, why are you cutting
into her from the side?

659
00:36:10,034 --> 00:36:13,371
If you approach from the farthest
place from the spine,

660
00:36:13,437 --> 00:36:15,206
you're increasing the risks further!

661
00:36:15,306 --> 00:36:16,741
That sure is right!

662
00:36:17,008 --> 00:36:18,442
Hey, Daimon!

663
00:36:18,509 --> 00:36:23,981
Are you trying to kill the leader of
1.5 million nurses in Japan?

664
00:36:24,649 --> 00:36:27,118
You're the one who was
going to let her die!

665
00:36:27,251 --> 00:36:29,787
What are you talking about?

666
00:36:30,054 --> 00:36:31,389
Forget that!

667
00:36:31,455 --> 00:36:38,129
Explain why you're operating
from the side, you fool!

668
00:36:38,396 --> 00:36:40,398
- Shut the hell up.
- Shut the hell up.

669
00:36:41,499 --> 00:36:46,003
<i>Women carry some secrets to their grave.</i>

670
00:36:50,274 --> 00:36:51,542
I can understand that.

671
00:36:53,311 --> 00:36:54,645
I understand.

672
00:37:08,926 --> 00:37:12,263
I never fail.

673
00:37:14,665 --> 00:37:17,401
<i>I fell in love with a patient.</i>

674
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:23,474
He was the only man in this world

675
00:37:24,008 --> 00:37:25,610
that I fell in love with.

676
00:37:26,611 --> 00:37:28,779
Is that the father of your son?

677
00:37:31,148 --> 00:37:35,353
He died before my son was born.

678
00:37:46,330 --> 00:37:50,034
I could never tell a single soul.

679
00:37:50,201 --> 00:37:52,203
Not my son. Not anyone.

680
00:37:54,205 --> 00:37:56,007
The man I loved was

681
00:37:56,540 --> 00:37:59,110
a gangster.

682
00:38:06,017 --> 00:38:07,518
<i>Why did you get a tattoo?</i>

683
00:38:09,053 --> 00:38:10,955
I was young.

684
00:38:15,559 --> 00:38:19,030
But I was serious about it back then.

685
00:38:21,565 --> 00:38:26,203
I wanted to engrave my body
with the memory of him.

686
00:38:37,648 --> 00:38:39,317
Excuse me.

687
00:38:40,718 --> 00:38:41,786
Vitals?

688
00:38:42,053 --> 00:38:45,523
BP, 110 over 73. Pulse, 80, sinus.

689
00:38:46,123 --> 00:38:47,158
Done.

690
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:57,768
<i>- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.</i>

691
00:39:03,708 --> 00:39:05,209
Well then,

692
00:39:05,609 --> 00:39:09,080
shall we return to the restaurant,
Shigekatsu?

693
00:39:18,989 --> 00:39:20,491
I don't really understand it,

694
00:39:22,093 --> 00:39:23,527
but that sure was awesome.

695
00:39:27,365 --> 00:39:28,766
Dr. Daimon!

696
00:39:30,901 --> 00:39:33,771
That was a magnificent operation.
Thank you.

697
00:39:36,340 --> 00:39:39,443
You're a full-fledged nurse now. Nice job.

698
00:39:41,645 --> 00:39:43,414
Thank you!

699
00:39:54,725 --> 00:39:56,494
Thank you.

700
00:39:56,560 --> 00:39:58,396
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

701
00:40:13,477 --> 00:40:15,513
This feels so nice!

702
00:40:15,613 --> 00:40:17,248
That was cold of you,

703
00:40:17,348 --> 00:40:20,217
operating like that without telling me.

704
00:40:21,519 --> 00:40:23,788
Michiko, are you listening?

705
00:40:25,222 --> 00:40:26,624
Michiko!

706
00:40:46,544 --> 00:40:48,646
What? It was just a sticker?

707
00:40:52,116 --> 00:40:53,584
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

708
00:40:54,318 --> 00:40:56,720
Director Hiruma, the usual person is here.

709
00:40:56,821 --> 00:40:59,056
The usual person? Who's that?

710
00:41:00,157 --> 00:41:02,026
Oh, it's the melon guy.

711
00:41:02,092 --> 00:41:04,094
- Excuse me.
- It's okay.

712
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:07,465
- Here's the usual melon.
- Right.

713
00:41:10,468 --> 00:41:12,436
This is the bill.

714
00:41:13,571 --> 00:41:16,273
Hold on a minute here.

715
00:41:16,407 --> 00:41:19,743
Your two freelance doctors,

716
00:41:20,177 --> 00:41:24,248
they operated secretly
without permission, you know.

717
00:41:24,348 --> 00:41:28,118
There's no way I'm paying you
for an operation like that.

718
00:41:30,054 --> 00:41:33,624
The election for chairman of
the Japan Physicians Club is coming up.

719
00:41:34,325 --> 00:41:39,330
You must be glad you obtained
the immense trust of Kasuga no Tsubone.

720
00:41:39,430 --> 00:41:42,132
I'm rooting for you as well.

721
00:41:44,835 --> 00:41:46,804
Is this a watermelon?

722
00:41:53,244 --> 00:41:54,311
CERTAIN VICTORY

723
00:41:54,378 --> 00:41:56,280
A certain victory Daruma.

724
00:41:57,481 --> 00:41:59,216
Let me have a look at this.

725
00:42:04,154 --> 00:42:05,656
That's a lot.

726
00:42:06,290 --> 00:42:08,292
- You scared me.
- Certain victory!

727
00:42:12,263 --> 00:42:13,531
I'll pay.

728
00:42:14,064 --> 00:42:16,200
I got it!

729
00:42:16,267 --> 00:42:18,435
Twenty million!

730
00:42:22,773 --> 00:42:24,575
Hello? Michiko?

731
00:42:25,042 --> 00:42:27,511
Stop by the private room on your way out.

732
00:42:27,578 --> 00:42:30,548
What? Overtime?

733
00:42:30,714 --> 00:42:34,018
Kasuga no Tsubone says
she wants to thank you.

734
00:42:34,118 --> 00:42:39,123
If it goes well, you can get back
what you lost on Rat Coin, yes?

735
00:42:39,823 --> 00:42:43,060
- Seriously?
- See you later.

736
00:42:45,829 --> 00:42:48,499
Here I go!

737
00:42:49,333 --> 00:42:51,535
Sorry!

738
00:42:53,337 --> 00:42:54,838
Excuse me.

739
00:42:56,173 --> 00:42:58,309
I'm sorry to call you here so late.

740
00:42:58,709 --> 00:43:00,411
You're checking out tomorrow, right?

741
00:43:00,611 --> 00:43:04,181
Your surgical skills
are truly magnificent.

742
00:43:04,848 --> 00:43:06,417
I get that a lot.

743
00:43:06,483 --> 00:43:08,752
I wanted to thank you before going.

744
00:43:09,987 --> 00:43:14,124
If you want to give me those huge,
lame clothes, I don't want it!

745
00:43:14,391 --> 00:43:15,893
No.

746
00:43:34,178 --> 00:43:35,646
Amazing!

747
00:43:35,713 --> 00:43:38,382
GORO

748
00:43:41,619 --> 00:43:45,489
You protected it without damaging
a single millimeter.

749
00:43:46,523 --> 00:43:47,725
Thank you.

750
00:43:49,793 --> 00:43:51,295
You're welcome.

751
00:44:00,471 --> 00:44:03,507
Masako quit the girly bar, Nurse Station?

752
00:44:03,574 --> 00:44:06,343
Yes. She's going to stick with
her true profession from now on.

753
00:44:06,410 --> 00:44:07,745
I can't call her by her first name.

754
00:44:07,978 --> 00:44:10,280
- Masako...
- Wrong. That's sexual harassment.

755
00:44:10,347 --> 00:44:12,516
They got a new girl to replace her.

756
00:44:12,616 --> 00:44:14,118
Her name's Maria.

757
00:44:15,219 --> 00:44:17,421
Okay. Let's leave on time again today.

758
00:44:18,722 --> 00:44:20,457
You're in my way!

759
00:44:20,524 --> 00:44:23,394
- <i>She hates groups, hates authority,</i>
- Michiko...

760
00:44:23,460 --> 00:44:25,062
<i>and hates restrictions.</i>

761
00:44:25,796 --> 00:44:29,266
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

762
00:44:29,433 --> 00:44:31,101
<i>are her weapons.</i>

763
00:44:31,702 --> 00:44:34,271
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

764
00:44:34,338 --> 00:44:37,041
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

765
00:44:57,528 --> 00:44:59,163
I'd like that doctor
to operate on this girl.

766
00:44:59,229 --> 00:45:00,197
One hundred billion?

767
00:45:00,264 --> 00:45:02,466
<i>Using a child's illness
for publicity's sake.</i>

768
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:04,635
If I don't do it, the patient will die.

769
